WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.020
In 221 BCE, the Xianyang Palace awoke in the golden morning light.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.460
The young Qin Shi Huang resolved to unify the six states that very year.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:14.780
Qin's black banners fluttered in the wind as the great army marched east.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.100
One state after another surrendered — the world was unified.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.100
Qin Shi Huang gathered scholars and unified the different scripts of the states into small-seal script.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.320
The scholars wrote earnestly — from then on, everyone used the same writing.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:37.260
Craftsmen cast round copper coins, and merchants traded with unified weights and measures.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:43.860
The whole country used the same money and scales, and people's lives became much easier.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.350
Although the Qin dynasty lasted only a short fifteen years,

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:53.260
its unified systems had a far-reaching influence, becoming a turning point in Chinese history.

